## User Story

**As a** DevOps engineer / developer,
**I want** the MongoDB Compass Web UI (isidata.satuinbox.com) to connect without timeout errors,
**So that** I can manage and inspect MongoDB databases for the SatuInbox omnichannel platform.

---

## Problem

The MongoDB Compass Web UI at `https://isidata.satuinbox.com` was experiencing connection timeout issues when attempting to browse databases and run queries. Users were unable to interact with MongoDB through the web interface.

## Root Cause Analysis

**Location:** `/app/omnichannel-satuinbox/dev/mongo-web/` on sidev server

### Investigation Steps

1. **Container Status** — `compass-web-satuinbox` container was running (Up, healthy), using image `haohanyang/compass-web:latest` on port 8080.
2. **MongoDB Connectivity** — Direct connection test from inside the container to MongoDB at `192.168.27.149:30941` was successful (ping OK).
3. **Local Access** — `curl http://localhost:8080` returned HTTP 200 in ~17ms — the app itself was fine.
4. **Nginx Proxy** — The reverse proxy config at `/etc/nginx/sites-available/dev-v2.satuinbox.com` for `isidata.satuinbox.com` was **missing critical settings**:
   - No WebSocket upgrade headers (`Upgrade`, `Connection`)
   - No proxy timeout configuration (defaulting to nginx 60s timeout)
   - Missing semicolon after `server_name` directive

### Root Cause

Compass Web uses **WebSocket connections** for real-time MongoDB operations (browsing databases, running queries, streaming results). The nginx reverse proxy was not forwarding WebSocket upgrade requests, causing the browser-side connection to timeout.

## Fix Applied

Updated the nginx server block for `isidata.satuinbox.com` in `/etc/nginx/sites-available/dev-v2.satuinbox.com`:

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name isidata.satuinbox.com isidata.satuinbox.dev;
    client_max_body_size 20M;
    client_body_buffer_size 20M;
    location / {
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;
        proxy_redirect off;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;
        proxy_send_timeout 300s;
        proxy_connect_timeout 60s;
    }
}
```

### Changes Made
- Added `proxy_http_version 1.1` — required for WebSocket
- Added `Upgrade` and `Connection` headers — enables WebSocket passthrough
- Added `X-Real-IP`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Forwarded-Proto` — proper proxy headers
- Added `proxy_read_timeout 300s` — allows long-running queries (5 min)
- Added `proxy_send_timeout 300s` — allows large data transfers
- Added `proxy_connect_timeout 60s` — connection establishment timeout
- Fixed missing semicolon after `server_name`

### Backup
Original config backed up at: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/dev-v2.satuinbox.com.bak.20260406112052`

## Verification
- `nginx -t` — config syntax OK
- `systemctl reload nginx` — applied successfully
- External HTTPS access — HTTP 200 in ~87ms
- Local proxy access — HTTP 200 in ~3ms

# Memory Leak Fixes

## 🔴 Issues Identified

### 1\. `checkSessions` doesn't force recreate _(Critical)_

**File:** `session.service.ts` ~line 180

```typescript
// ❌ BUG: session.currentContext doesn't have force: true
await this.createSession(session.currentContext);
```

When a disconnected session is detected, `createSession` is called without `force: true`, so the broken session is returned instead of being destroyed and recreated.

### 2\. Unread messages in Redis have no TTL

**File:** `baileys.service.ts` ~line 389

```typescript
// ❌ No TTL - accumulates forever
await this.deps.cache.rpush(redisKey, JSON.stringify(msg.key));
```

### 3\. Connection service doesn't clean up before reinit

**File:** `whatsapp-connection.service.ts` ~line 196

```typescript
// ❌ Old socket/authState/lidMappingStore not nulled before new one
await this.initializeSocket();
```

## ✅ Fixes Applied

### Fix 1 — Force recreate in `checkSessions`

**File:** `session.service.ts` ~line 180

```typescript
// Before
await this.createSession(session.currentContext);

// After
await this.createSession({ ...session.currentContext, force: true });
```

### Fix 2 — Add TTL to unread messages in Redis

**File:** `baileys.service.ts` — `storeUnreadMessage`

```typescript
// Added TTL to prevent memory accumulation
await this.deps.cache.expire(redisKey, CacheTTLEnum.ONE_DAY);
```

### Fix 3 — Add cleanup before reinit in connection service

**File:** `whatsapp-connection.service.ts` — new `cleanup()` method

```typescript
private cleanup(): void {
  if (this.sock) {
    this.removeAllListeners();
    this.sock.ws?.close();
    this.sock.end(new Error(ERROR_MESSAGE.CONNECTION_CLOSE));
    this.sock = null;
  }
  this.authState = null;
  this.lidMappingStore = null;
}
```

### Fix 4 — Improve `onModuleDestroy` in `BaileysService`

**File:** `baileys.service.ts` — `onModuleDestroy`

```typescript
// Added cleanup for GC
this.authState = null;
this.lidMapingStore = null;
```

